-- title:
--   Stochastic continuity gives strong continuity for a full process
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a topological group and let $\nu$ be a stationary probability law on the canonical coordinate space $\mathbb R^G$. Write $X_g(\omega)=\omega(g)$. If
--
--   $$\lim_{g\to1}\nu\{|X_g-X_1|\ge\varepsilon\}=0\qquad\text{for every }\varepsilon>0,$$
--
--   then the canonical shift representation of $G$ on $L^2(\mathbb R^G,\nu)$ is strongly continuous: for every $F\in L^2(\nu)$ the map $g\mapsto U_gF$ is norm continuous. The sigma-algebra is generated by all process coordinates, so this also describes any full realization modulo null sets. No second-moment assumption on the coordinates is required. This gives the converse continuity implication for full stationary processes.
-- source:
--   Reflection Positive Stochastic Processes Indexed by Lie Groups, arXiv:1510.07445v3, PDF p. 44, Lemma A.4

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Gap48_P06

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter

open scoped Topology ENNReal NNReal

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P06

/-- Lemma A.4, PDF p.44: for a full real stationary process, continuity in
measure implies strong continuity of the canonical L2 representation. Fullness
is enforced by the canonical coordinate sigma-algebra; square integrability
of coordinates is not assumed. -/
theorem stationaryProcess_strongContinuity
    {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]
    (nu : Measure (G → ℝ)) [IsProbabilityMeasure nu]
    (hstationary : ∀ g, MeasurePreserving (pathShift g) nu nu)
    (hmeasure : ∀ eps : ℝ, 0 < eps →
      Tendsto (fun g => nu {w | eps ≤ |w g - w 1|}) (𝓝 (1 : G)) (𝓝 0)) :
    ∀ f, Continuous (fun g => pathKoopman nu hstationary g f) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P06

end
